WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.518 --> 00:00:03.785
- [Narrator] Meet Onyx, a five-year-old

00:00:03.785 --> 00:00:05.251
eastern indigo snake.

00:00:05.251 --> 00:00:08.763
(dramatic music)

00:00:08.763 --> 00:00:11.182
At nine feet in length, eastern indigos

00:00:11.182 --> 00:00:12.740
are considered to be the longest

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.645
native snakes in the United States.

00:00:15.645 --> 00:00:17.951
Even though they lack a venomous bite,

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:21.379
they can fall victim to
overzealous rattlesnake hunters,

00:00:21.379 --> 00:00:24.367
as they inhabit the same burrows.

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:26.618
Their beautiful, smooth-scaled skin

00:00:26.618 --> 00:00:29.641
is a shade of bluish black.

00:00:29.641 --> 00:00:32.229
Carnivorous, like all snakes, Onyx feeds

00:00:32.229 --> 00:00:36.143
on any small animal she can overpower.

00:00:36.143 --> 00:00:39.080
Onyx may hiss or rattle
her tail when alarmed,

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.868
but she'll hardly ever bite.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:45.154
Like most snakes, humans
are their biggest threat,

00:00:45.154 --> 00:00:48.267
as continued urbanization
has left them threatened

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:51.608
throughout parts of the United States.

00:00:51.608 --> 00:00:54.358
This is the eastern indigo snake.

